      "content": "It's understandable to want to feel better quickly after a tough workout, but taking 2000mg of potassium chloride all at once is a very large dose that can be dangerous. High doses of potassium can disrupt your heart rhythm, so it's much safer to use lower, recommended dosages from your supplement. For immediate cramping relief, try a balanced electrolyte drink with sodium and potassium in smaller amounts instead.",
