      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if you feel severely depleted, a massive, immediate intake like 2000mg of supplemental potassium is risky and can lead to serious health issues. Electrolyte loss is complex; while potassium is important, you also need sodium and fluids for proper recovery. To help you feel better safely, opt for a well-formulated sports drink or an electrolyte powder that contains balanced amounts of essential minerals rather than a huge dose of only potassium.",
      "source": "target",
